{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide takes you from a wired Swidux app to a fully gated feature with paywall presentation, entitlement observation, restore, and manage-subscription support. It covers state and action wiring, implementing a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":", presenting the sheet, gating a feature, and previewing in pro state.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference of every type and action, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","text":"Before you start","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a Swidux app already wired up — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You have a purchase backend in mind. RevenueCat is the path of least resistance, but vanilla StoreKit or a custom server work just as well — the plugin doesn’t care."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPaywall\",","    ]",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Step-2-Add-state-and-actions","text":"Step 2: Add state and actions","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add a paywall slice to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"text":", and a paywall case to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ AppState.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var paywall: PaywallState = .init()","    \/\/ … other slices","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["\/\/ AppAction.swift","import SwiduxPaywall","","enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case paywall(PaywallAction)","    \/\/ … other cases","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin owns reducing for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall"},{"text":" actions, so the root reducer should fall through:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ AppReducer.swift","case .paywall:","    return nil"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Step-3-Provide-a-PaywallService","text":"Step 3: Provide a `PaywallService`","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The plugin needs a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" conformer that talks to your purchase backend. Pick the path that matches your backend.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Path-A-RevenueCat-recommended","text":"Path A: RevenueCat (recommended)","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" companion package and use the supplied ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RevenueCatPaywallService"},{"text":". No bridging code on your side.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\", from: \"1.0.0\"),"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["import SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","","let service = RevenueCatPaywallService()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The companion package also ships ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI"},{"text":", a SwiftUI sheet built on RevenueCatUI that hands purchase results back through the plugin. See its README for configuration (API key, entitlement identifiers).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Path-B-StoreKit-or-custom-backend","text":"Path B: StoreKit or custom backend","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For any non-RevenueCat backend, implement ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService"},{"text":" directly. The protocol is small:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","struct MyPaywallService: PaywallService {","    func customerInfo() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Fetch the current entitlement once.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","","    func customerInfoStream() -> AsyncStream<EntitlementSnapshot> {","        AsyncStream { continuation in","            \/\/ Yield a new snapshot each time the entitlement changes.","            \/\/ Call continuation.finish() when the source ends.","        }","    }","","    func restorePurchases() async throws -> EntitlementSnapshot {","        \/\/ Run a restore against the user's account and return the result.","        return EntitlementSnapshot()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A vanilla StoreKit conformer iterates ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.currentEntitlements"},{"text":" and listens to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Transaction.updates"},{"text":"; a custom server conformer hits whatever endpoint reports the user’s entitlement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Previews-and-tests","text":"Previews and tests","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the built-in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"text":" for backend-agnostic previews:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let service = MockPaywallService(isPro: true)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re on Path A, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},{"text":" also ships ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService"},{"text":" for RevenueCat-flavored previews.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Step-4-Wire-the-plugin","text":"Step 4: Wire the plugin","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Construct and register ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallPlugin"},{"text":" inside your ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"text":" factory:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SwiduxPaywall","","let paywallPlugin = PaywallPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.paywall,","    action: AppAction.paywall,","    extractAction: { if case .paywall(let a) = $0 { return a }; return nil },","    service: RevenueCatPaywallService()",")","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Step-5-Observe-customer-info-on-launch","text":"Step 5: Observe customer info on launch","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Start the long-lived entitlement stream once, on the root view:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct ContentView: View {","    @Environment(AppStore.self) private var store","","    var body: some View {","        RootContent()","            .task { store.send(.paywall(.observeCustomerInfo)) }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeCustomerInfo"},{"type":"text","text":" returns an effect that lives for the duration of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PaywallService.customerInfoStream()"},{"type":"text","text":". Every snapshot the service yields flows through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":" and updates "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.isPro"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hasPermanentLicense"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Step-6-Present-the-paywall","type":"heading","text":"Step 6: Present the paywall"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bind a sheet to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.isPresented"},{"type":"text","text":" and dispatch "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall(.dismiss)"},{"type":"text","text":" when it closes:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".sheet(isPresented: Binding(","    get: { store.paywall.isPresented },","    set: { if !$0 { store.send(.paywall(.dismiss)) } }",")) {","    PaywallSheet()","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Trigger presentation by dispatching ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".paywall(.request(reason:))"},{"text":" with a short identifier describing why you’re asking. The reason is stored in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.requestedReason"},{"text":" so the sheet can tailor its copy.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))"]},{"anchor":"Step-7-Gate-a-feature","type":"heading","text":"Step 7: Gate a feature","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Read "},{"code":"PaywallState.isGateSatisfied","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" before running gated work. If it’s "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", dispatch "},{"code":".request","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Button(\"Export PDF\") {","    if store.paywall.isGateSatisfied {","        store.send(.export(.exportPDF))","    } else {","        store.send(.paywall(.request(reason: \"export-pdf\")))","    }","}"]},{"anchor":"Step-8-Restore-purchases","type":"heading","text":"Step 8: Restore purchases","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a restore button to your paywall sheet. Reflect "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.isLoading"},{"type":"text","text":" to disable it while the call is in flight:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Button(\"Restore Purchases\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.restorePurchases))","}",".disabled(store.paywall.isLoading)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On success, the resulting snapshot flows through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".customerInfoUpdated"},{"type":"text","text":" and updates the gate. On failure, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.paywall.error"},{"type":"text","text":" is set."}]},{"anchor":"Step-9-Manage-subscriptions","text":"Step 9: Manage subscriptions","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For an existing subscriber, surface a button that deep-links into the system subscription management page:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["Button(\"Manage Subscription\") {","    store.send(.paywall(.openManageSubscriptions))","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This opens "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"itms-apps:\/\/apps.apple.com\/account\/subscriptions"},{"type":"text","text":" via the plugin’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"openURL"},{"type":"text","text":" handler, which routes to the App Store on iOS and Settings on macOS."}]},{"anchor":"Testing","text":"Testing","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MockPaywallService"},{"type":"text","text":" to drive previews and tests into a known entitlement state:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["#Preview(\"Pro\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService(isPro: true)","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}","","#Preview(\"Free\") {","    let store = AppStore.configured(","        paywallService: MockPaywallService()","    )","    return ContentView().environment(store)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plumb the service through a parameter on your "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store.configured()"},{"type":"text","text":" factory so previews can override it without touching the live RevenueCat SDK."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Add a Paywall","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"https://github.com/heirloomlogic/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall":{"title":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"}],"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/heirloomlogic\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","title":"Add Feature Flags","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginPaywallReference":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginpaywallreference","abstract":[{"text":"API reference for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library — paywall presentation, entitlement observation, and purchase orchestration.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","role":"article","title":"SwiduxPaywall Reference"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","title":"Add Analytics","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","title":"Add a Version Killswitch","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","title":"Add a Parental Gate","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","type":"topic"}}}